"31149431-8f70-11ef-b074-507c6f2b8348,4589,21-10-2024 00:00,Site Office,Delhi,SOmp1,NULL,Project,IT,VPP,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,21-10-2024 11:19,195,""It is to bring your attention to an issue encountered during the processing of the 10th variation of the DC-02 contract on the VPP portal. It appears that the items listed in Schedule-C (Any Other DSR) and Schedule-B3 have not been assigned to their respective groups. This error (""""Items having different tax % or different % increase / % decrease cannot be assigned to same group"""") can be seen in the attached Screenshot-I."															
"It is worth mentioning that the same tax considerations were applied in previous variations, as documented in Screenshot-II. "															
															
"In view of above, it is kindly request your assistance in resolving this issue at your earliest convenience to expedite the approval process for this variation."															
"Email has already been sent to VPP support team."",2,Others,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,Error.png,NULL,""The existing items that were mapped to the groups and the new items that were being mapped had different in boq type, due to which the warning was coming and 2nd waring 100cr solution :- According to the business logic being applied, if any existing group contains more than 100CR amount items, the system will not allow the addition of new items to it and will not allow the transaction to proceed. So, Nodal has to create a new group and add respective items since the Old group capacity of 100CR is full. In the current issue, Amity added the new group and aligned items in it as discussed with the DMRC team."",NULL,NULL,1031,1031,NULL,1,0,2801,RAHUL SOHAL,NULL,523256,,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,2801,21-10-2024 11:19,21-10-2024 19:10,1031,182.74.205.42,NULL,5,NULL,0,0,0,,,NULL,NULL,0,1"															
