"7080423e-060f-11f0-a243-10153cebe7c2,11165,21-03-2025 00:00,Site Office,Delhi,SODKD1,NULL,Project,IT,Vendor Payment Portal,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,21-03-2025 10:16,197,""Invoice value does not match with claim raise on Vendor Payment Portal. For example claim quantity consider only up to third place of decimal due to this claim value lags in vendor payment portal  and amount mitch match with actual invoice."															
Earlier communication regarding above issue is as below:															
															
From: VPP Support [mailto:vpp.support@dmrc.org] 															
Sent: 18 July 2024 11:11															
To: rahulgarg@johnsonliftsltd.com															
Cc: DMRC DMRC; sourav sen; sdeb@johnsonliftsltd.com; Musharraf Hassan Kamal															
Subject: Re: DE-06 (Differance between VPP bill % &amp; our Bill)															
															
_/**/															
delivered quantity will only accept till 3 decimal number like 0.022 not 0.0223. So this is not feasible to do through the VPP portal.															
															
Regards															
															
VPP Support															
															
______________															
From: rahulgarg@johnsonliftsltd.com															
"To: """"VPP Support"""" "															
"Cc: """"DMRC DMRC"""" , """"sourav sen"""" , sdeb@johnsonliftsltd.com, """"Musharraf Hassan Kamal"""" "															
"Sent: Thursday, July 11, 2024 10:54:18 AM"															
Subject: RE: DE-06 (Differance between VPP bill % &amp; our Bill)															
															
Dear Sir/Madam															
 															
"I done the same, but the value (bill amount) is incorrect due to our delivered quantity is 0.0223, but the delivered quantity taken only 0.022."															
"As per VPP Invoice amount is Rs. 153745.68 and as per actual bill amount of Rs. 156166/- (Per Lift Price for One month of 179 Lifts : Rs. 69,88,440/179 = 39041.56 X 4 Lifts (To be billed)= 156166/-"															
 															
"if any possibility  to change the Bill % in VPP Portal. (2.23 actual bill % and VPP taken the % 2.20 or 2.30) if VPP take the bill% of 2.23, so that the bill may be matched. (screen shot attached)"															
 															
Please do the needful.															
 															
Dear Manish JI															
Please help  to do the same.															
 															
With regards															
RAHUL GARG															
 															
From: VPP Support [mailto:vpp.support@dmrc.org] 															
"Sent: Wednesday, July 10, 2024 5:08 PM"															
To: rahulgarg@johnsonliftsltd.com															
Cc: DMRC DMRC; sourav sen; sdeb@johnsonliftsltd.com; Musharraf Hassan Kamal															
Subject: Re: DE-06 (Differance between VPP bill % &amp; our Bill)															
 															
_/**/															
"Dear ,"															
"Kindly use only delivered quantity column to set the quality since Bill% column is just to show the percentage on the screen and will not affect the calculation part.  Delivered quantity column is the main and directly attached to the calculation, henceforth recommended to be used for billing transactions without considering what Bill% column is showing."															
 															
Regards															
															
VPP Support															
 															
______________															
From: rahulgarg@johnsonliftsltd.com															
"To: """"VPP Support"""" "															
"Cc: """"DMRC DMRC"""" , """"sourav sen"""" , sdeb@johnsonliftsltd.com, """"Musharraf Hassan Kamal"""" "															
"Sent: Wednesday, July 10, 2024 1:42:39 PM"															
Subject: RE: DE-06 (Differance between VPP bill % &amp; our Bill)															
 															
Dear Sir/madam															
 															
"As per your trailing mail, as per your instructions we follow the same, but there is automatic changes in delivered quantity while we add the bill % (2.23) without click on the delivered quantity, it will automatically changed i.e 0.022. (Screenshot attached)"															
 															
With regards															
RAHUL GARG															
9911000404															
 															
 															
From: VPP Support [mailto:vpp.support@dmrc.org] 															
"Sent: Tuesday, July 09, 2024 5:05 PM"															
To: rahulgarg@johnsonliftsltd.com															
Cc: DMRC DMRC; sourav sen; sdeb@johnsonliftsltd.com; Musharraf Hassan Kamal															
Subject: Re: DE-06 (Differance between VPP bill % &amp; our Bill)															
 															
_/**/															
As we can see the user is being taken 2.23 Bill % for which system is calculating delivered quantity ( 0.022 ) but in case the user clicks on delivered quantity again then the bill % value will set 2.30 as a round off value. So please inform user to not click on the delivered qty textbox after filling-up value on bill %.															
 															
Regards															
															
VPP Support															
 															
______________															
From: rahulgarg@johnsonliftsltd.com															
"To: """"VPP Support"""" "															
"Cc: """"DMRC DMRC"""" , """"sourav sen"""" , sdeb@johnsonliftsltd.com, """"Musharraf Hassan Kamal"""" "															
"Sent: Tuesday, July 9, 2024 11:27:05 AM"															
Subject: DE-06 (Differance between VPP bill % &amp; our Bill)															
 															
Dear Sir/Madam															
 															
We are trying to submit a bill on VPP portal for DE-06 Contract for 04 lifts at Krishna Park Metro Station.															
 															
"But in VPP portal in RA without abstract Bill, in row of Bill% - quantity taken only first place of decimal (2.20) but our Claim % is 2.23 and further quantity taken 2.30 (there is value not taken in between 2.20 to 2.30)."															
 															
"Now, claim value less as actual, attached screen shot for your reference."															
 															
Please resolve this issue ASAP…so that we can raise the bill as per actual quantity.															
 															
With regards															
RAHUL GARG															
